Name: Phishy Business
Level: High School
Difficulty: Easy
Topic: Social Engineering
Software Required: None

This challenge involved looking at a series of emails and the player must be able to know if
it's suspicious or not. If said email is suspicious, you must choose the correct social 
engineering technique being used. This will involve using provided sources to detect social engineering 
such as ChatGPT or the sources provided in this python game. Run the application file and if you 
get all the answers correct, then you will recieve the flag. The flag is the 
ID number of each of the suspicous all combined into one string, so keep up with you 
answers. Hopefully, you walk away from this challenge with more knowledge of social engineering. Go Phish!

Flag Example: ictf{12345678910111213}

